    <briefdescription>
<para>Specify the latency in cpu cycles for a particular scheduling class and def index. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>-1 indicates an invalid latency. Heuristics would typically consider an instruction with invalid latency to have infinite latency. Also identify the WriteResources of this def. When the operand expands to a sequence of writes, this <ref refid="namespacellvm_1_1_calling_conv_1abdf8cf606905c10634e831390981b0ed" kindref="member">ID</ref> is the last write in the sequence. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
